. * Further data preparation: calculating unpaid work hours and merging partner
> 's hours and sex
. 
.         // Our preferred measure of gender equality in the household ("as mea
> sured by behaviors or outcomes" is 
.         // the difference in weekly unpaid work hours between father and fema
> le partner (which need not be the mother of the father's children), 
.         // calculated as the father's hours minus the partner's hours, so hig
> her values mean greater egalitarianism. 
.         // Unpaid work hours are calculated as the sum of reported average we
> ekly hours spent on housework, errands/shopping, and repairs.
.         // Weekly hours for each partner are calculated as:
.         // 5 times reported average housework/errands/repairs hours on weekda
> ys 
.         //       + reported average housework/errands/repairs hours on Sunday
> s
.         //       + reported average housework/errands/repairs hours on Saturd
> ays. 
. 
